{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And pardon our iniquity and our sin, and take us as Your inheritance.</b> Because of Moses' great humility he included himself with them, for he should have said 'their iniquity and their sin' (לעונם ולחטאתם). And Jeremiah, who was of his tribe, learned from him, for he said (Jeremiah 14:7): ״אם עונינו ענו בנו ה' עשה למען שמך״ — 'Though our iniquities testify against us, O HaShem, act for Your name's sake' — and he did not say 'their iniquities' (עונם). And he said ונחלתנו ('and make us Your inheritance') when he should have said ותנחילנו ('and You shall make us inherit'), but its meaning is: that You should make us inherit, so that we become Your inheritance — and this is the word of the prophet who said (Lamentations 3:24): ״חלקי ה' אמרה נפשי על כן אוחיל לו״ — 'The portion of HaShem, says my soul; therefore I will hope in Him.' Scripture says: 'my soul says, the portion of HaShem is my lot' — that is, I have no portion in the earth except for the service of the Blessed Name, which is my portion; therefore I will hope in Him, that we may be allotted to His portion. This is what Scripture says (Deuteronomy 32:9): ״כי חלק ה' עמו״ — 'For the portion of HaShem is His people.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:55.859603103Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}